   "k": "2m0cy0",
   "en": "Equipment variants are concrete, country-specific classes of ⟦0⟧ which are based on an equipment type. They may include customizations such as ⟦1⟧, upgrades, or modules.",
   "frags": 2
  },
  {
   "k": "1la4po7",
   "en": "equipment"
  },
  {
   "k": "1emgqq8",
   "en": "design companies"
  },
  {
   "k": "19phq7s",
   "en": "Base"
  },
  {
   "k": "u3azz3",
   "en": "When a country unlocks an equipment type by researching the corresponding technology, a base variant of it gets created. Where applicable, it uses the design company the country has at that moment. It is not necessary to already have the design company when the research starts."
  },
  {
   "k": "1inmx8d",
   "en": "Module"
  },
  {
   "k": "142dz7t",
   "en": "Main articles: Tank designer, Ship designer"
  },
  {
   "k": "130892b",
   "en": "Main article: Aircraft designer"
  },
  {
   "k": "r32jg5",
   "en": "In games where the tank/ship/plane designer are enabled (with the appropriate DLC), equipment modules can be changed to create new variants of a specific model (for example, changing an engine within a tank)."
  },
  {
   "k": "c8df8n",
   "en": "Modules extend the capabilities of an equipment variant in a more detailed manner than upgrades. Ship hulls, tank chassis, and plane airframes act as a base equipment types offering a number of module slots that can be used. The hulls, chassis, and airframes are researched individually and can mix different (researched) modules to create variants at the cost of naval/army/air experience in the appropriate designer. Without ⟦0⟧ nor ⟦1⟧, researched ship & tank equipment types automatically combine ship hulls and tank chassis and a standard configuration of modules that cannot be changed.",
   "frags": 2
  },
  {
   "k": "1hpzefz",
   "en": "Man the Guns"
  },
  {
   "k": "11r223j",
   "en": "No Step Back"
  },
  {
   "k": "11uemf",
   "en": "Equipment upgrade"
  },
  {
   "k": "c3ogug",
   "en": "In games where the tank/ship/plane designer are disabled, there are several types of equipment which can have specific attributes upgraded using experience. Sometimes a small improvement in speed, protection, or firepower can make a significant difference in the field."
  },
  {
   "k": "iz2ua3",
   "en": "Variants are expensive in XP, so their use should take into account the expected benefit, production volume, and service lifetime of the variant in deciding where to commit these resources. This is especially important for capital ships, as they take a very long time to build and there are large year-gaps between models."
  },
  {
   "k": "199d303",
   "en": "Each upgrade may be selected up to five times and may be made at different times. Existing equipment upgrades may be viewed in the Production screen. Upgrades in one area may reduce performance in another area - e.g., complexity reducing reliability or increased weight-reducing speed. Note that land units may use maintenance support companies that increase reliability for equipment in that division, and also that equipment stats and performance may also be affected by government staff with particular skills that provide modifiers."
  },
